  "slug": "graph-cherti",
  "title": "–GRAPH — CHERTI",
  "summary": "Iskra Velitchkova explores the relationship between physical and software drawings in \"CHERTI,\" constantly moving between code and physical materials to understand their behavior and output. She notes that the constraints of physical drawing make her \"more aware of how much we can learn from technology and its capacity to produce complexity.\" The web browser displays a detailed window of the software drawing, while the physical drawing reveals the whole composition; both views are shown together to convey this relationship.<br/>\"CHERTI\" is a software NFT. The first collector of each edition receives the corresponding plotter drawing, shipped directly from the artist’s studio. The software NFT and plotter drawing are not linked; the NFT can continue to be collected on a secondary market without the drawing. Users can generate a new image by clicking the artwork or pressing the spacebar. Press ‘1’ to zoom out, ‘2’ to zoom in, and ‘3’ to return to original magnification.<br/>The main artwork page on Feral File displays the plotter drawing for the artist-proof (AP). Compare this to the corresponding software version of the AP to see their relation. Software and physical drawings are \"delightfully different\" due to the range of papers and inks used. Digital editions feature two randomly selected color schemes, but physical drawings associated with the editions will have the same colors and match the AP.<br/>The \"CHERTI\" drawings are 50 × 70 cm (19.8 × 27.6 inches) on ivory Fabriano Rosaspina 220 gsm paper, drawn with black, brown, and red Muji Gel Ink pens.",
  "coverImage": "https://imagedelivery.net/5BJzhBHeVhlhbn58hvcXAQ/cfca9c98-6ead-4800-1bdf-8801399f0000/raw",
